      "text": "1. JS SEO Basics",
      "size": "lg",
      "color": "ink",
      "opacity": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Google uses an <strong>evergreen Chromium</strong> to render pages.",
        "<strong>Rendering Workflow</strong>: Crawl -&gt; Render Queue -&gt; Render -&gt; Index.",
        "<strong>Lazy-loading</strong>: Google supports native lazy-loading (<code>loading=\"lazy\"</code>). Ensure content is in the viewport when rendered."
      ],
      "size": "md",
      "color": "ink",
      "opacity": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "2. Dynamic Rendering",
      "size": "lg",
      "color": "ink",
      "opacity": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "<strong>Status</strong>: Workaround, not a long-term solution.",
        "<strong>Recommendation</strong>: Use Server-Side Rendering (SSR), Static Rendering, or Hydration."
      ],
      "size": "md",
      "color": "ink",
      "opacity": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "3. SPA & Routing",
      "size": "lg",
      "color": "ink",
      "opacity": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Avoid hash-based routing (<code>#/</code>) for critical content as Google may not crawl fragments.",
        "Use the <strong>History API</strong> (Clean URLs) for Single Page Applications."
      ],
      "size": "md",
      "color": "ink",
      "opacity": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "4. Web Components & Shadow DOM",
      "size": "lg",
      "color": "ink",
      "opacity": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Google can index content in the Shadow DOM, but it's best to use Light DOM for critical SEO content to ensure maximum compatibility."
      ],
      "size": "md",
      "color": "ink",
      "opacity": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "5. App Shell Architecture",
      "size": "lg",
      "color": "ink",
      "opacity": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Avoid serving a generic App Shell for every URL if it delays content discovery. Ensure the meaningful content is available quickly."
      ],
      "size": "md",
